WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:18.175
Under International rules, any vessel other than a vessel not under command or a vessel restricted in her ability to maneuver shall, if circumstances admit, avoid impeding the safe passage of a vessel constrained by her draft that is showing the signals of Rule twenty-eight.

2
00:00:18.425 --> 00:00:26.100
The vessel constrained by her draft shall navigate with particular caution, having full regard to her special condition.

3
00:00:26.350 --> 00:00:31.450
Remember from Rule eight that not impeding means acting early to leave sea room.

4
00:00:31.700 --> 00:00:34.475
It’s different from give-way and stand-on.

5
00:00:34.725 --> 00:00:39.825
And remember that constrained by draft doesn’t exist under Inland rules.
